WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:04.099
Ivan Vasilev.

2
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.160
Madam President, Mr Minister,

3
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.060
Your Excellencies,

4
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.350
Mr Deputy Mayor, dear organisers,

5
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.840
dear friends and guests, it is a pleasure for me to take part in

6
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.920
the opening of the first Black Sea Technology Forum, right here in

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.820
Varna.

8
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.480
Technology without borders. This forum's motto sounds like a promise of

9
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.310
the future, but it actually describes the present.

10
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:04.350
Technology has long had no borders.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.360
We are the ones who have borders, and they usually lie in the speed

12
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:13.309
at which we make decisions, finance ideas and implement innovations.

13
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.840
I thank the Applied Research and Communications Fund, ICT Cluster

14
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.399
Varna, who made this forum possible, Varna Municipality

15
00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:47.520
for hosting it, and the Executive Agency for the Promotion of

16
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.110
Small and Medium-sized Enterprises for its support.

17
00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.439
I also thank the ambassadors of France, Belgium and the Kingdom of

18
00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:59.280
the Netherlands. Your presence here matters greatly to us and to

19
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.629
our shared innovation future in Europe.

20
00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:28.069
The question this forum asks itself is a direct one.

21
00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:32.800
Will the Black Sea region be a pole of growth in the European

22
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.470
artificial intelligence economy, or only a consumer of it?

23
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.720
The answer is not predetermined, so I will allow myself to be specific

24
00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.990
about both the strengths and the deficits.

25
00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.480
I come to the Ministry of Innovation and Digital Transformation from

26
00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.750
the entrepreneurial community, and I am used to speaking and acting this way.

27
00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:28.599
Varna has engineering and software talent.

28
00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:31.750
Four universities, including the naval academy,

29
00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:35.200
a large European Union port on the Black Sea,

30
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.670
an active ICT cluster and a digital innovation hub, according to the transatlantic

31
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.830
innovation competitiveness index.

32
00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.080
Varna is Bulgaria's second European region in terms of

33
00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.750
development potential. That is a serious foundation.

34
00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:21.440
but the same index also shows something else.

35
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.340
Productivity

36
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.240
of labour in Bulgaria remains at around 110 of the European Union

37
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.479
average. This is not a statistic we hide.

38
00:04:30.479 --> 00:04:33.070
And that is also why all of us have gathered here.

39
00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.960
A few days ago I was with President Iotova at the ceremony for

40
00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.230
the John Atanasoff awards.

41
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:55.400
Bulgaria develops exceptional talent in the field of information

42
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.550
technology and digitalisation.

43
00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.600
The question before us is how we keep them, how we bring them back and how we

44
00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.309
use them for the prosperity of the country and the region.

45
00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.400
What are we doing on these topics?

46
00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.430
First, we are changing the rules.

47
00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:36.400
The variable capital company now gives Bulgarian start-ups

48
00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.749
a legal form that the international investor recognises,

49
00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.950
without the company having to register elsewhere.

50
00:05:43.479 --> 00:05:46.550
I also created a special council on innovation and technological development,

51
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.400
so that together with business we can set out the concrete steps and

52
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.000
administrative changes that will make Bulgaria the best

53
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.600
place to start and grow high-value-added business

54
00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.749
in Europe by 2030.

55
00:06:34.599 --> 00:06:38.400
We are building a new national model for knowledge and technology transfer,

56
00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.960
a coordinating centre and a decentralised network of technology

57
00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.149
transfer offices in scientific and innovation institutions.

58
00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.039
My position is that the region, with Varna's universities and industry,

59
00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:51.390
must be among the first in this network.

60
00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:15.160
Bulgaria is home to BRAIN++, one of the six new AI factories

61
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.800
of the European Union, with an investment of 90 million

62
00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.080
euros and a new supercomputer attached to it.

63
00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.360
This is computing capacity that has never existed before in

64
00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.990
this region.

65
00:07:40.639 --> 00:07:43.440
Digital transformation and the introduction of artificial intelligence

66
00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.879
that people can trust is the next thing

67
00:07:45.879 --> 00:07:50.080
we are doing. My commitment as minister is that relations between

68
00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.800
the state, citizens and business become easy,

69
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.639
fast and convenient. Ethical AI is the condition for this goal to

70
00:07:58.639 --> 00:07:59.539
be achieved.

71
00:08:21.759 --> 00:08:24.240
And one more thing that is part of innovation policy,

72
00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:26.159
even though it is not called that.

73
00:08:26.159 --> 00:08:29.879
In June this year it became clear that over 30% of the public

74
00:08:29.879 --> 00:08:33.110
procurement contracts awarded in our country had only a single bidder.

75
00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:37.039
The Sigma platform made public spending visible,

76
00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:39.110
and what is visible is easier to fix.

77
00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.509
I am saying this at this forum on purpose.

78
00:08:41.959 --> 00:08:45.160
Public demand is one of the largest markets for technology

79
00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.360
companies in Europe. Closed, it cannot be offset by

80
00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:54.000
any subsidy. Open, it can be the strongest innovation

81
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:58.519
programme. I also support the European Commission's efforts in this direction

82
00:08:58.519 --> 00:09:02.519
to make public resources more competitive and accessible to

83
00:09:02.519 --> 00:09:04.750
innovative technology companies.

84
00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.839
Ladies and gentlemen, none of this happens only within

85
00:09:55.839 --> 00:10:00.160
national frameworks; it is inseparably linked to our shared European

86
00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.030
future, as the programme of today's forum shows.

87
00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.680
Recently, Bulgarian space technologies were presented at

88
00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:08.310
the highest level in Paris.

89
00:10:08.839 --> 00:10:12.590
With France we are linked by the two European AI models,

90
00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.360
Mistral and BGPT. Bulgaria is ready to take part in the international

91
00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.839
formats of the OECD and the US Pax Silica,

92
00:10:20.839 --> 00:10:24.760
which are building trusted technology supply chains and common

93
00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:27.640
security standards with the European Union.

94
00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:31.760
For Europe to be technologically strong, competitive and reliable

95
00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.760
on the global stage, a clearer link is needed between scientific

96
00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.920
research, computing infrastructure, funding and

97
00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:41.110
industrial deployment.

98
00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:38.160
Speaking of connectivity, the Black Sea plays a key and strategic

99
00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.389
role in the connectivity of Bulgaria and Europe.

100
00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.440
In transport, in energy, and very soon, I am sure,

101
00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:46.430
digitally too.

102
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.040
We are actively working to establish Bulgaria as a digital hub on

103
00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:05.279
the East-West axis, using our strategic

104
00:12:05.279 --> 00:12:08.920
geographic position and developing our role in European and

105
00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.959
transregional routes for data transfer,

106
00:12:11.959 --> 00:12:13.920
including through the Black Sea.

107
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.920
The Trans-Caspian data corridor, already being built in

108
00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:21.440
Kazakhstan and, I hope, passing through the Black Sea in 2027 and

109
00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:25.040
reaching Sofia, will raise the speed of data exchange between

110
00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:29.880
East and West and, through Bulgaria, will make the entire European Union

111
00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.639
more connected in the emerging economy based on knowledge,

112
00:12:34.639 --> 00:12:36.430
data and computing power.

113
00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.320
And finally, I would like to conclude by noting

114
00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.389
that Bulgaria is already measuring up to the most advanced.

115
00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:27.279
Our country is part of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology

116
00:13:27.279 --> 00:13:30.110
programme for developing regional innovation ecosystems.

117
00:13:30.519 --> 00:13:34.560
And at the end of January 2027 we will host the global

118
00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:35.949
cohort of this programme.

119
00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.320
On the same days the National Innovation Forum will also take place,

120
00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:42.040
where the anniversary annual report Innovations.BG

121
00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.920
of the Applied Research and Communications Fund will be presented,

122
00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.000
dedicated to 20 years of Bulgaria's membership of the European Union.

123
00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:52.279
Whatever is agreed here over these three days of the conference,

124
00:13:52.279 --> 00:13:55.680
can be continued four months later, again with

125
00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:56.829
international partners.

126
00:14:38.519 --> 00:14:42.519
I am sure that Bulgaria can lead in the technological revolution

127
00:14:42.519 --> 00:14:44.550
that will change the world we live in.

128
00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.590
I wish all of you successful work.

129
00:15:20.199 --> 00:15:22.990
Madam President, Mr Minister,

130
00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.120
Mr Regional Governor, Mr

131
00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:31.399
Deputy Mayor, Your Excellencies, dear guests of this

132
00:15:31.399 --> 00:15:34.959
wonderful forum. It is a great pleasure for me to be here, and as

133
00:15:34.959 --> 00:15:38.910
at every forum, I walked among the participants and asked them

134
00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:42.389
whether they like the idea, what they want to achieve,

135
00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:48.309
where we are heading. The answers were more than thought-provoking.

136
00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:53.110
In fact, Varna is hungry for this type of event.

137
00:15:53.639 --> 00:15:59.120
A full hall with so many people willing to share and learn.

138
00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:02.279
It is rarely seen. And perhaps this is the moment to thank the

139
00:16:02.279 --> 00:16:05.480
organisers too. Congratulations on the wonderful event

140
00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.380
you have organised.

141
00:16:53.519 --> 00:16:57.519
And as we joked with Minister Vasilev, this is the first edition of

142
00:16:57.519 --> 00:17:00.560
the forum. We hope you will invite us to the 50th.

143
00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:04.439
We will be at the back with our canes, but we will support you just as much

144
00:17:04.439 --> 00:17:05.389
as we do now.

145
00:17:24.199 --> 00:17:27.760
I am the Minister of Tourism and I would like to say a few words about

146
00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:31.349
how much technology means for tourism.

147
00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.670
You know that in Bulgaria tourism holds,

148
00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.160
I would say, one of the leading places in our economy,

149
00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:43.630
with 8% direct impact and about 14% indirect.

150
00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:49.520
For the city of Varna it represents perhaps a little over 35% of

151
00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.360
the economy. So the place for this forum is here, and the topic of tourism

152
00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:59.390
is here too.

153
00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:28.679
First, let me tell you a story so you understand where we are starting from.

154
00:18:28.679 --> 00:18:34.000
In 1999 I started working in tourism and, like any young person of

155
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:38.000
16, I really wanted to work by the sea.

156
00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.709
There, 15 of us fought for one place.

157
00:18:41.679 --> 00:18:46.360
15 people wanted to work, whether in a restaurant,

158
00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:51.520
a bar or a hotel. And where was our sector then?

159
00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.919
How digitalised was it?

160
00:18:52.919 --> 00:18:57.679
Not at all. The head chef wrote on loose sheets of paper.

161
00:18:57.679 --> 00:19:01.679
Often there were no products on the menu because someone had simply lost

162
00:19:01.679 --> 00:19:05.400
the notebook where it said what he needed for the next day.

163
00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:09.039
The barman did not even want to be digitalised,

164
00:19:09.039 --> 00:19:12.720
because he wrote the bills in little notebooks and handed them to tourists.

165
00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:16.720
And do you know how surprised I was when I had to help

166
00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:20.360
the receptionists and they gave me a sketch of the hotel and

167
00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:24.559
felt-tip pens in different colours, to colour in the rooms,

168
00:19:24.559 --> 00:19:27.070
the occupied ones, according to the tourists' nationality.

169
00:20:48.799 --> 00:20:52.310
Today, things have advanced so much

170
00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:57.159
that we have different software solutions along the whole supply chain.

171
00:20:57.159 --> 00:21:00.240
Starting with the apps each of you checks on your phone

172
00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.440
to decide where to go, the marketing channels,

173
00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:06.640
the information-gathering channels, the sales funnels,

174
00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:11.270
continuing with online tour operators, which currently hold over 40%

175
00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:16.030
of bookings, and only three companies hold 85%

176
00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:22.120
of all reservations. We're talking about online tour operators like Booking,

177
00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:25.910
Expedia and Trip.com.

178
00:21:27.039 --> 00:21:31.760
Then the various systems that help manage

179
00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:34.520
the hotel. Moving on to digital menus.

180
00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:38.960
Then the assistants you'll find in hotel rooms,

181
00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.120
which help you order better.

182
00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:44.310
We optimize processes in the kitchen, restaurant and bar.

183
00:21:44.799 --> 00:21:47.150
Moving on to repeat sales,

184
00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:51.120
on to assessing tourists' opinions, and many, many

185
00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:54.960
more solutions. You can see how far technology has penetrated

186
00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:55.860
our sector.

187
00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:16.910
And despite everything, we keep measuring

188
00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:20.150
quantity, not quality.

189
00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:26.000
And here our government has made a very important decision,

190
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.679
to stop talking only about quantity and turn to the qualitative

191
00:23:29.679 --> 00:23:31.640
side as well. And what did we do?

192
00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:36.159
Just days ago, on 27 September, World Tourism Day,

193
00:23:36.159 --> 00:23:40.159
we founded an Association of Universities Studying Tourism here

194
00:23:40.159 --> 00:23:44.910
in Varna. It is unique in Europe as an organization,

195
00:23:46.039 --> 00:23:52.720
a phenomenon, and an observatory was set up alongside it to measure

196
00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:56.200
tourists' satisfaction with their stay in Bulgaria.

197
00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:58.360
It will measure over 200 criteria.

198
00:23:58.360 --> 00:24:02.109
There will be huge room here for innovation, for new technologies,

199
00:24:02.559 --> 00:24:06.880
which scientists, doctoral students and students themselves can practise

200
00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:11.919
in real life, and finally the deputy mayor, the mayor or the minister,

201
00:24:11.919 --> 00:24:16.159
whoever it is, when we ask: you track overnight stays well,

202
00:24:16.159 --> 00:24:19.799
revenues, but what about your quality, will be able to answer,

203
00:24:19.799 --> 00:24:23.480
because what we can measure, we can improve,

204
00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:28.880
and that is just what we want: to measure in order to improve. Finally,

205
00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:30.880
I would like to say something. I see you are taking notes,

206
00:24:30.880 --> 00:24:32.550
so you will read it at the end.

207
00:24:33.159 --> 00:24:36.919
Finally, I'd like to say something we constantly say in tourism:

208
00:24:36.919 --> 00:24:39.440
no matter how far technology advances,

209
00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:43.960
no matter how much we develop, human care, human attitude

210
00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:48.520
must come first. So don't just talk about tourism,

211
00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:51.399
don't just work with tourism, but consume it as well.

212
00:24:51.399 --> 00:24:52.750
I wish the forum every success.
